&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operations Analyst&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Executive Planning &amp;amp; Operations team solves critical strategy, planning, and execution challenges across Fastly. We are looking for a curious and proactive Operations Analyst to partner with leadership in Engineering, Product Management, Analytics, Finance, Program Management, Product &amp;amp; Engineering Operations, and others to develop and manage engineering, financial, and technical processes, execute key operational cadences, and drive successful business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and mature multiple key cross-organizational processes including Product Lifecycle, Engineering Ops, software capitalization, and others&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operationalize and mature emerging processes around FinOps and cloud spend management&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instill discipline and consistency within the Product and Engineering teams in terms of operational methodologies and documentation, working with Senior Director &amp;amp; VP level resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with cross-functional resources as primary point of contact to improve communications, enhance visibility, and measure results of different strategic portfolios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion tooling and process improvements that help the team and Fastly scale&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years in business operations or other key functions including business process improvement, and product or engineering teams (bonus points for both)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail within big picture context&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead team initiatives by influence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience effectively communicating across multiple levels including distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focus on results and outcome, not just process for process sake&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong action bias, preference for execution and incremental improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to document and train a variety of stakeholders on new and revised processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A history of putting structure around ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’ll be super impressed if you have experience in any of these:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with engineering in a Tech organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leveraging AI to automate and scale&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting to executives and leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to ​​independently plan and execute on multiple strategic initiatives or projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Functional knowledge of financial, sales, or other core business metrics; experience with program management methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Hours:&lt;/strong&gt; This position will require you to be available during core business hours.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Location(s) &amp;amp; Travel Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt; This position is open to the following preferred office locations:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;San Francisco, CA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Denver, CO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;New York City, NY&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
