&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fastly helps people stay better connected with the things they love. Fastly’s edge cloud platform enables customers to create great digital experiences quickly, securely, and reliably by processing, serving, and securing our customers’ applications as close to their end-users as possible — at the edge of the Internet. The platform is designed to take advantage of the modern internet, to be programmable, and to support agile software development. Fastly’s customers include many of the world’s most prominent companies, including GitHub, Yelp, Paramount, and JetBlue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re building a more trustworthy Internet. Come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The Sales Support Analyst -Tier 1, will be part of Fastly’s Global Sales Operations team, providing Tier 1 Sales Operations support for International Sales teams in AMERICAS. They will partner closely with the Tier 1 Sales Operations lead and AMERICAS Field operations team, as well as multiple stakeholders across Channel and SE operations, Marketing operations, and IT Business Systems teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be an entry-level Sales Operations role, and will report into the Director, Global Sales Strategy &amp;amp; Operations, based out of our India office. This role will also matrix into the Tier 1 Sales Operations lead based out of our Denver office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The perfect candidate for this role is a self-starter, curious, and willing to learn new things quickly. They will have at least 1-2 years business experience, ideally in a Support or Sales related role (Sales rep, SDR/BDR, CSM, sales operations). Preferred experience with high-tech or SaaS based companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;They will have a foundation in analytical and problem solving skills, able to compile basic data analysis using Excel or Google sheets. They will also have previous experience leveraging AI capabilities to improve productivity and efficiency.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Tier 1 Sales Operations lead in setting the foundation for an optimized Tier 1 support model, with a focus on AMERICAS sales team support. They will do this through process documentation, managing and responding to sales inquiries within defined SLAs, and triaging and escalating to Tier 2 support level teams (Field, Channel and SE operations) as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for managing defined Tier 1 scope related sales inquiries from the AMERICAS teams. For any other inquiries, they will escalate to the appropriate Tier 2 support teams (Field, Channel and SE operations teams).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;May assist AMERICAS sales operations teams with basic sales operations tasks including data hygiene tasks, account and lead routing validation, and basic reporting in SFDC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;May assist with new hire onboarding for Salesforce CRM and Sales tools, partnering with the Tier 1 Sales Operations Support lead and Sales Enablement teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-2+ years of Support or Sales/Sales operations experience, ideally at a high-tech or SaaS based company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and willingness to learn new things quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and using agentic-prompts to automate workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic Excel or Google sheets skills to compile simple business analysis.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred to have prior experience using CRM (Salesforce) and other basic sales tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
