&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fastly helps people stay better connected with the things they love. Fastly’s edge cloud platform enables customers to create great digital experiences quickly, securely, and reliably by processing, serving, and securing our customers’ applications as close to their end-users as possible — at the edge of the Internet. The platform is designed to take advantage of the modern internet, to be programmable, and to support agile software development. Fastly’s customers include many of the world’s most prominent companies, including GitHub, Yelp, Paramount, and JetBlue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re building a more trustworthy Internet. Come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technology Compliance Lead (FedRAMP) - Security&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;As a Technology Compliance Lead (FedRAMP), you will help scale Fastly’s technology compliance program to meet the needs of a FedRAMP program. This is a unique opportunity to develop a new program from the ground up. You will own and lead from start to finish a program to meet FedRAMP’s new 20x program, collaborating with people both inside and outside the organization, including department heads, engineers, auditors, and customers. This position will report to the Director, Technology Compliance and will work closely with partners across the organization, including Customer Success, Security, Engineering, Sales, Program Management, and Human Resources.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Maintain a deep understanding of our platform and its supporting infrastructure and processes, as well as how our compliance obligations apply to that environment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Collaborate across departments to develop and maintain controls that meet FedRAMP requirements as well as make sense for our business and existing compliance programs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Partner closely with program management and cross-functional groups to drive FedRAMP control implementation, continuous monitoring, and programmatic processes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Actively identify and communicate control gaps; help the company develop and confirm remediation efforts&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Liaise with external auditors and internal partners to facilitate audit procedures and evidence gathering&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Support third party oversight processes, including security and compliance assessments of Fastly’s vendors and service providers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Participate in FedRAMP community activities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;You have 5-7 years of security or compliance analysis, or assurance/advisory experience, including a focus on FedRAMP operations and leading programs as an individual contributor&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;You have experience mapping and rationalizing controls to meet requirements across multiple information security/technology compliance standards (e.g., PCI DSS, HIPAA, ISO 27001, SOC 1/ SOC 2, FedRAMP)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;You have a thorough understanding of technical environments, and the ability to communicate with subject matter experts about technical and operational security controls&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;You hold a BS degree in Management Information Systems, Computer Science, or a related field&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;You have excellent written and verbal communication skills to communicate details of a security program to a wide spectrum of audiences, including customers and senior leadership&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;You have strong analytical skills and attention to detail&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;You have the ability to be self-directed and take initiative on projects and tasks, directing others and in identifying gaps related to security controls, with minimal day-to-day oversight/direction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #172b4d;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We value a variety of voices, so this is not a laundry list. It would be an added bonus if you have experience in ANY of these:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;CISA, CISM, CISSP, or related certification&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Experience using governance, risk management, and compliance (GRC) tools, especially FedRAMP trust centers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: #000000 !important;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #000000;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with the FedRAMP 20x modernization framework and requirements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
